### D6. The `ab_arm` comment

The old reason, that a row with two different arms at two arguments is not
expressible because one port function answers for all of them, is false: the
port has type `forall R idx, SecurityPort (amf_sample f R idx)`, whose result
type does not mention the constructor, so a function may return one
constructor at one index and the other at another. What actually prevents it
is that `certify_exact` and `certify_spectral` are the only statements that
build a port and each writes one constructor at every argument. The comment
now states that fact about the statements. No counter-example was compiled:
no instance of the tree holds both an `ExactWitness` and a `SpectralCert` over
one sample adapter, so the branching port cannot be written today.

